{
  "abstract": "Transverse momentum spectra of $\\pi^{\\pm}$, $p$ and $\\bar{p}$ up to 12 GeV/c at mid-rapidity in centrality selected Au+Au collisions at $\\sqrt{s_{_{NN}}} = 200$ GeV are presented. In central Au+Au collisions, both $\\pi^{\\pm}$ and $p(\\bar{p})$ show significant suppression with respect to binary scaling at $p_T > $ 4 GeV/c. Protons and anti-protons are less suppressed than $\\pi^{\\pm}$, in the range 1.5 $< p_{T} <$6 GeV/c. The $\\pi^-/\\pi^+$ and $\\bar{p}/p$ ratios show at most a weak $p_T$ dependence and no significant centrality dependence. The $p/\\pi$ ratios in central Au+Au collisions approach the values in p+p and d+Au collisions at $p_T >$ 5 GeV/c. The results at high $p_T$ indicate that the partonic sources of $\\pi^{\\pm}$, $p$ and $\\bar{p}$ have similar energy loss when traversing the nuclear medium.",
  "access_urls": {
